 "bloques": [
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Leave the job",
   "texto": [
    "**уволиться** (quit) is used to leave a job voluntarily. To say «leave work» in the sense of leaving the place, **уйти с работы**: **Я ухожу с работы в пять** is used (I leave work at 5: 00). **Увольнение** appoints the end of employment: it can be voluntary or by decision of the company, so it does not always mean «dismissal».",
    "**Перейти** (pass) goes with **на**: **перейти на другую работу** (move to another job)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "They gave me and offered me",
   "texto": [
    "With **дать** (give) the person you receive goes in dative: **Мне дали отпуск** (I was given a vacation). With **предложить** (offer) it is the same: **Мне предложили новую работу** (offered me a new job).",
    "**Собираться** + infinitive expresses a plan or an intention; it does not in itself indicate that the action will occur immediately: **Я собираюсь уволиться** (I intend to leave the work). The perfect **начать** forms the simple future **начну**: **я начну работать** (I will start working)."
   ]
  },
